    "message": "feat(admin): make the guide readable and the analytics denser\n\nThree changes, all inside the existing palette and layout language.\n\nThe guide was the worst of it. .guide-body capped the whole column at\n78ch, and .guide-shot was width:100% of that cap, so every screenshot\nrendered at roughly 600px -- these are captures of a full dashboard, so\nthe UI inside them was illegible, while two thirds of the page sat\nempty. Prose and figures want different widths, so they now get them:\nthe column runs to 1180px and only the running text is held at 74ch.\nScreenshots render at the full column width and open at full size on\nclick, with Esc or a click to dismiss, reachable by keyboard, and\ncaptioned from their existing alt text. Body text goes to 15px/1.7,\ncallouts are no longer dimmed to muted grey, and section headings carry\na rule so the twelve sections are separable while scrolling. The\ncontents list marks the section you are actually reading.\n\nAnalytics gained numbers rather than losing them. Stats now aggregate\ntool calls, turns using tools, and turns with reasoning, each shown with\nits share of the window. The request detail header goes from 8 fields to\n19: key, uncached input, cached input, cache writes, per-request cache\nhit rate, output rate in tokens/sec measured after first token, and a\none-line summary of the turn's shape.\n\nThe reasoning pane now uses the --info blue that was already in the\ntoken set instead of the violet added in the previous commit, so the\npalette stays exactly as wide as it was.\n\nVerification: 5/5 local CI; 3101 passed, same 14 failures as the\nunmodified base. Rendered against the real assets and the real\nscreenshots at 1600px and 414px: no horizontal overflow, guide images\nmeasured at 1180px (was 598px) with prose held at 598px, lightbox opens\nand returns focus, contents list tracks the scrolled section.\n\nKnown and not addressed: the bundled guide screenshots still show the\nv4.15.0 UI, so they predate both the emerald charts and the new request\ndetail. Refreshing them needs a live server with real data.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
